on would prefer B. However, the individual chose A. Thus, the reason, as stated, would not prefer A. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable — the information (outcomes and probabilities) is available and the sum of pairwise differences can be computed. The reason is clearly applicable to this decision problem.",
