  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the lotteries. The only non-zero outcome difference is -6000 - (-3000) = -3000. The sum of pairwise differences is -3000. The reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less negative) sum of outcome differences. Since this sum is negative and applies only to A relative to B, the sum is more favorable for B (as it has a smaller loss). However, the individual in the verbal report does not mention the pairwise differences in outcomes or their sum. Instead, the individual focuses on the probability of loss and incorrectly claims the expected loss is lower in B (it is actually equal). The justification is based on intuitive risk perception and expected value (misapplied), not on the sum of pairwise outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The required information (sum of pairwise outcome differences) is not present in the report, and the justification does not follow the rule of the reason.",
